From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 19:49:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a finished animation that fills forwards, and recascade
 on cancel

`process_animations_for_style` removed every finished animation from
the element's set. For `animation-fill-mode: forwards` or `both` that
throws away a contribution the element is still entitled to: the value
is right in the resolve the animation finishes in, and wrong on the
next restyle of that element, whatever triggered it. Anything whose
only visible state came from a fill snapped back to its cascaded value.
For example, a lazy loader that fades images in over a base
`opacity: 0` goes transparent again the first time the page writes a
style.

`get_property_declaration_at_time` already honours the fill, so keeping
the animation in the set is enough; it is retired the usual way when
the element stops specifying it. Fold the duplicated fill-mode
predicate into `Animation::fills_forwards`, since both call sites need
it.

Cancelling has to mark the set dirty, or the fill can never be removed.
Dropping `animation-name` sets `AnimationState::Canceled`, but
`process_animations` only recascades when `ElementAnimationSet::dirty`
is set, and this loop never set it, while `cancel_active_transitions`
and `cancel_all_animations` both do. Mark it dirty in the same resolve,
before `clear_canceled_animations` sweeps the entry and the set
disappears.

All three hunks should land upstream in servo/stylo.
---
 matching.rs        |  8 +++++---
 servo/animation.rs | 17 +++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/matching.rs b/matching.rs
index 4aae362..1e7f954 100644
--- a/matching.rs
+++ b/matching.rs
@@ -768,9 +768,11 @@ trait PrivateMatchMethods: TElement {
             .transitions
             .retain(|transition| transition.state != AnimationState::Finished);

-        animation_set
-            .animations
-            .retain(|animation| animation.state != AnimationState::Finished);
+        // A forwards fill outlives the run it belongs to, so that animation is
+        // still the element's authority for its properties. Keep it.
+        animation_set.animations.retain(|animation| {
+            animation.state != AnimationState::Finished || animation.fills_forwards()
+        });

         // If the ElementAnimationSet is empty, and don't store it in order to
         // save memory and to avoid extra processing later.
diff --git a/servo/animation.rs b/servo/animation.rs
index 8376bd7..567efe0 100644
--- a/servo/animation.rs
+++ b/servo/animation.rs
@@ -616,6 +616,15 @@ impl Animation {
         new_ui.animation_duration_mod(index).seconds() == 0.
     }

+    /// Whether this animation keeps applying its final keyframe once it has
+    /// ended, per `animation-fill-mode`.
+    pub fn fills_forwards(&self) -> bool {
+        matches!(
+            self.fill_mode,
+            AnimationFillMode::Forwards | AnimationFillMode::Both
+        )
+    }
+
     /// Given the current time, advances this animation to the next iteration,
     /// updates times, and then toggles the direction if appropriate. Otherwise
     /// does nothing. Returns true if this animation has iterated.
@@ -862,10 +871,7 @@ impl Animation {
         {
             return;
         }
-        if self.has_ended(now)
-            && self.fill_mode != AnimationFillMode::Forwards
-            && self.fill_mode != AnimationFillMode::Both
-        {
+        if self.has_ended(now) && !self.fills_forwards() {
             return;
         }

@@ -1297,5 +1303,8 @@ impl ElementAnimationSet {
         for animation in self.animations.iter_mut() {
             if animation.is_cancelled_in_new_style(new_style) {
                 animation.state = AnimationState::Canceled;
+                // Cancelling drops this animation's declarations, so the caller
+                // has to recascade, as with `cancel_active_transitions`.
+                self.dirty = true;
             }
         }
